VVIf you want the cleaner version going forward, use su - t9amail (with the dash) — that loads t9amail's own environment and drops you in /home/t9amail automatically.
T9AMAIL

Project to provide a web-based email 'client' for use on HMD feature phone.
Main limit is Opera Mini Extreme mode.
Cannot realistically browse to likes of www.gmail
Solution: web page interface optimised for Opera Mini and 2.4" screen
Framework: 
- mbsync runs (cron) and stores a persistent  INBOX on vps
- bottle + scripts render a usable html interface
- IMAP calls only required for sending mail
- mail service: posteo
∗∗∗∗∗∗∗∗∗∗∗∗∗


# mbsync posteo to local (see ~/.mbsyncrc) 
- include ~/Mail/Inbox/cur & new

# REPLY
- browse inboxes
- create RFC.eml from selected UID 
- send with msmtp < RFC.eml

# see ~/.msmtprc

